# Clear Zenith / Cloudy Horizon — layout studies

Status: unapproved layout concepts, generated with built-in image_gen. Black denotes empty sky; these previews are not opacity masks or packed engine textures. No Unreal import or level assignment.

A: balanced peripheral banks. B: asymmetric large masses. C: layered distant horizon. All preserve open zenith and inward-facing crowns.

## A_BalancedBanks

Use case: stylized-concept. Create ONE square polar UV CLOUD LAYOUT STUDY, not a landscape view. Pure black background for empty sky, cloud shapes off-white with only subtle broad gray planes, simple readable silhouette concept, not final detailed texture. Circle centered on canvas, radius 46% of width, leave corners black. Center represents zenith and outer radius horizon. Central clear-sky disk at least 55% of circle radius entirely EMPTY black. Clouds mostly within radial range 0.65 to 0.98; occasional larger bank crown reaches 0.56. Every crown and bright face points INWARD toward center, undersides point OUTWARD toward rim: at 12 o'clock crown faces down, at 3 left, at 6 up, at 9 right. Cloud long axes follow local circumference, never radial streaks or spiral. Populate outer horizon with abundant cloud banks of varied angular lengths and radial depths: several substantial cumulus masses and smaller distant low cloud clusters mixed among them, coherent size hierarchy and irregular gaps. Large smooth connected cloud lobes with restrained unevenness, broad flattened undersides outward. NO sawtooth edges, no uniform scallop beads, no wispy speckle confetti, no outlines, no text, no diagram lines, no uniform donut, no central clouds. Keep all clouds fully within canvas. Composition A: Balanced broken horizon belt. Four unequal major banks distributed around the outer circle, separated by distinct blue-sky-equivalent black gaps. Smaller distant banks fill some intervening rim segments. About 75% of horizon circumference cloudy, 25% interrupted. Fairly balanced around all azimuths but never identical repeated forms. Very wide clear zenith.

## B_AsymmetricMass

Use case: stylized-concept. Create ONE square polar UV CLOUD LAYOUT STUDY, not a landscape view. Pure black background for empty sky, cloud shapes off-white with only subtle broad gray planes, simple readable silhouette concept, not final detailed texture. Circle centered on canvas, radius 46% of width, leave corners black. Center represents zenith and outer radius horizon. Central clear-sky disk at least 55% of circle radius entirely EMPTY black. Clouds mostly within radial range 0.65 to 0.98; occasional larger bank crown reaches 0.56. Every crown and bright face points INWARD toward center, undersides point OUTWARD toward rim: at 12 o'clock crown faces down, at 3 left, at 6 up, at 9 right. Cloud long axes follow local circumference, never radial streaks or spiral. Populate outer horizon with abundant cloud banks of varied angular lengths and radial depths: several substantial cumulus masses and smaller distant low cloud clusters mixed among them, coherent size hierarchy and irregular gaps. Large smooth connected cloud lobes with restrained unevenness, broad flattened undersides outward. NO sawtooth edges, no uniform scallop beads, no wispy speckle confetti, no outlines, no text, no diagram lines, no uniform donut, no central clouds. Keep all clouds fully within canvas. Composition B: Strong asymmetrical horizon composition. One broad substantial bank along lower-left through bottom quadrant, second medium bank upper-right, remaining rim has small low distant banks and two generous angular openings. Large banks remain peripheral; do not intrude into central clear disk. About 65% rim circumference cloudy. A clear focal mass with airy opposite side.

## C_LayeredHorizon

Use case: stylized-concept. Create ONE square polar UV CLOUD LAYOUT STUDY, not a landscape view. Pure black background for empty sky, cloud shapes off-white with only subtle broad gray planes, simple readable silhouette concept, not final detailed texture. Circle centered on canvas, radius 46% of width, leave corners black. Center represents zenith and outer radius horizon. Central clear-sky disk at least 55% of circle radius entirely EMPTY black. Clouds mostly within radial range 0.65 to 0.98; occasional larger bank crown reaches 0.56. Every crown and bright face points INWARD toward center, undersides point OUTWARD toward rim: at 12 o'clock crown faces down, at 3 left, at 6 up, at 9 right. Cloud long axes follow local circumference, never radial streaks or spiral. Populate outer horizon with abundant cloud banks of varied angular lengths and radial depths: several substantial cumulus masses and smaller distant low cloud clusters mixed among them, coherent size hierarchy and irregular gaps. Large smooth connected cloud lobes with restrained unevenness, broad flattened undersides outward. NO sawtooth edges, no uniform scallop beads, no wispy speckle confetti, no outlines, no text, no diagram lines, no uniform donut, no central clouds. Keep all clouds fully within canvas. Composition C: Dense distant layered horizon. Many low elongated outermost banks merge into 3 loose archipelagos with gaps, with three thicker larger cumulus groups slightly inward at unequal positions. Small distant clouds overlap behind larger foreground banks in just selected sectors, not two concentric solid rings. About 85% of rim circumference occupied but center widest and clearest of all, cloud material stays mostly beyond radius 0.72. Strong near/far size contrast without noisy tiny fragments.
